  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, but I couldn't run it or fully typecheck it. `@aura3d/engine` is missing from node_modules in this sandbox, so `typecheck` reports only \"Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'\". Calls into the engine are unchecked, and I wrote them from the docs.\n\n**Scene and camera:** `looks.preset(\"outdoor-day\")` supplies sky, lighting and shadows. The soil plot is 20×13 with wooden edging. A fixed perspective camera at (0, 11, 16), looking at (0, 0, 0.5), shows the whole plot.\n\n**Planting:** A click is mapped to the ground by intersecting the camera ray with the y=0 plane. The code assumes the engine's 45° fov is vertical, which I couldn't confirm. If the engine treats it as horizontal, planted spots will be off from the click. Clicks outside the plot are ignored.\n\n**Growth:**\n- Plants come from a pool of 80 pre-built nodes, because I found no documented way to add nodes after mount. If all 80 are in use, the oldest plant is recycled.\n- Each plant grows over 8 seconds of real time, using its own start time, so later plants are smaller.\n- A sprout is a thin stem with two tiny leaves. At maturity it has a tall stem, large leaves, and a flower disc with a centre, with the flower appearing after about 40% growth.\n- Flower colour comes from 8 colours, and height, leaf size and flower size vary per plant.\n\n**Overlay and globals:** The 'Plants: N' label and 'Clear' button sit in the top-left corner. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is a read-only getter, `window.__plantAt(x, z)` follows the same path as a click, and `__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame.\n\n**Untested engine calls:** I assumed `setScale(x, y, z)` and `setVisible(bool)` exist on node handles. If `setScale` only takes one number, stems and leaves would scale uniformly and look wrong. If `setVisible` is missing, unused plants stay parked at y = -60 instead of being hidden. I haven't checked that 80 plants with shadows hold a smooth frame rate.",
